<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Francis Warren</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born 1942</span> · Also known as James Warren</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James Francis Warren is an American-born historian of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a>, long based at Murdoch University in Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>. His book The Sulu Zone, 1768–1898 (1981) showed how the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> trade drew the Sulu Sultanate into a system of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slave-raiding">slave raiding</a> and labour, and he has also written social histories of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a> and of maritime raiding.</p></div>
